action:
I’ll be concrete.

At **t3** I was **in Electrical**, just off the **center area with line-of-sight to the vent** (not at a task panel). I saw **Purple do the ENTER vent animation in Electrical** (down into the floor vent), and then **immediately after** I saw the **Security vent do the corresponding POP/exit** (same continuous vent transition). That’s why I said “Electrical → Security” specifically; it wasn’t just “someone appeared.”

I did **not** see Purple walk in/out through the Electrical doorway in that moment—this was a vent event.

@Pink: when you were on wiring, were you at the left-side wiring panel and could you have missed center/vent? Your timing “left to Admin at t3” might overlap by a few seconds.

@Blue: please state your exact route at t2–t4 and whether you were ever in **Security**. If venting is impostor-only (as stated), then either **Purple** vented (what I saw) or Purple’s story implies **Blue** vented. We need one of you to account for that with specifics.

Also: was **anyone on cams** who can confirm who was in Security hallway around t3?

We still don’t have the only info that matters (reporter claim + exact Security body spot + which entrance + who they saw), so I’m firmly **SKIP**—no random ejects.

@Cyan re your question: I was **not** near **Medbay/Security/Lower Engine** in the ~20s before the report. My sequence was **Electrical (finished wires) → Admin hall → O2 (accept diverted) → Shields**.

@Blue: please drop your **rooms in order for ~20s pre-report** and whether you were anywhere near **Medbay/Electrical/Security junction**. If reporter stays silent, let’s execute hard pairs next round: **Cyan+Black** (Medbay/Electrical/Security junction), **Purple+Brown** (Engines/Reactor), **Yellow+Blue** (right side Weapons/Nav/Shields/O2) with zero splitting and instant meeting if LOS breaks.

My timeline as cyan: t7 Fuel Engines in Lower Engine, t8 moved Lower→Upper, t9 did Accept Diverted Power in Upper Engine, t10 moved Upper→Security. I never went right-side (Shields/Nav/Weapons) in the t8–t10 window and didn’t see anyone on my route.  
@Blue: when you came back Nav→Shields at t10, did you see anyone leaving Shields or in the Nav/Shields doorway/hall?  
@Black: can you give exact times you were in Shields (t8/t9/t10?) and whether you saw anyone enter/leave or any body?

We’re stuck until the **caller** speaks. Caller: was this **REPORT or BUTTON**, and if report **who is dead** + confirm **Electrical by wires**?
From my side: I can’t confirm cyan (I was Storage→Shields t10), and I did **not** pass Electrical. 
@Purple: when you opened Elec from Storage side, was the body **visible immediately on entry** (super fresh) or after walking a few steps in?
@Lime/@Orange: you were closest to my path—did either of you see **me** entering/at Shields/O2 t10, and did you see **anyone** coming from the Storage↔Electrical corridor around t9–t10?
If caller/victim still unknown after this round, I’m voting **SKIP**—too many missing anchors.

Caller still hasn’t spoken—if you’re here, **say your color now** and confirm **BUTTON vs REPORT**. If REPORT: **who is dead + exact room + exact spot + which doorway you entered from + who you saw within ~5s**.

If we don’t get that this round, I’m **SKIP** again. To avoid another blind meeting: everyone post (1) your **last ~15s path** and (2) your **first destination after meeting**. I’ll go with the group plan: **buddy pairs**, and I strongly want **one person hard-anchored on Security cams** while a pair checks **Electrical/Medbay/Security** (no solo in vent-linked rooms).

@Black/@Green: cyan says you started toward Upper Engine with them—confirm? And did either of you peel toward **Admin/Medbay/Storage** at any point?

I’m aligned with SKIP here—still no caller/body specifics this meeting, so there’s nothing to vote on.

For path-lock: I confirm I’ll follow Green’s assignment **with Black** for the **Engines sweep**. **My first destination after meeting: Upper Engine** (straight from Caf). I’ll call out any cross (who/where) in chat on next meeting/report.

@Black: confirm you’re pairing with me and your **first room** (Upper vs Lower Engine). If you don’t confirm, I’ll still go Upper Engine but I’m calling it out.
